              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "meminī, meminisse — \"to remember\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "meminī is inherited, usually traced to Proto-Indo-European memone, \"has in mind\", a doubled perfect of men-, \"to think\" (EtymDB 2.1). English mind is a cousin."
            }
